id: pm-57ir3b
title: "GH-752: list results claim completeness while unreadable items are omitted"
description: "Make list-family and SDK query results fail closed or expose structured unreadable-item incompleteness, and report decoder compatibility evidence without misattributing environment drift to item corruption."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: context,github,integrity,sdk,storage
created_at: "2026-07-26T19:39:00.227Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T19:39:00.227Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "List-family CLI, SDK, and MCP result contracts expose structured completeness and unreadable counts; strict behavior is available without token-heavy parsing; decoder version/range diagnostics distinguish dependency drift; regression tests cover pagination and all-status reads; docs and contracts are updated."
parent: pm-doxj
risk: high
confidence: high
reporter: GitHub #752
severity: high
expected_result: Agents and SDK consumers can mechanically distinguish a complete item set from a partial result whenever any item cannot be decoded.
actual_result: "Unreadable items are omitted while count, total, has_more:false, and truncated:false still present the filtered result as complete; only a warning string signals loss."
affected_version: 2026.7.26
component: list/query integrity
customer_impact: Agents can make planning and mutation decisions from a silently incomplete workspace view.
